<article class="env-lemma" id="0D4H">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D4H">Lemma <span data-tag="0D4H">37.30.4</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a flat morphism of schemes of finite presentation. Let $n_{X/Y}$ be the function on $Y$ giving the dimension of fibres of $f$ introduced in Lemma <a href="/tag/05F8" data-tag="05F8">37.30.2</a>. Then $n_{X/Y}$ is lower semi-continuous. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $W \subset X$, $W = \coprod _{d \geq 0} U_ d$ be the open constructed in Lemmas <a href="/tag/045U" data-tag="045U">37.22.7</a> and <a href="/tag/054T" data-tag="054T">37.22.9</a>. Let $y \in Y$ be a point. If $n_{X/Y}(y) = \dim (X_ y) = n$, then $y$ is in the image of $U_ n \to Y$. By Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01UA" data-tag="01UA">29.26.10</a> we see that $f(U_ n)$ is open in $Y$. Hence there is an open neighbourhood of $y$ where $n_{X/Y}$ is $\geq n$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>